    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d448">

                <pb facs="0556" n="548" xml:id="pg548"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.2331/228: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Peru</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Norweb</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-12-23T14:00:00-05:00">December 23, 1941—2
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>546. Reference Embassy’s telegram no. 668, of December 9. Please ascertain
                    whether Peruvian Government is agreeable to issuance of public notice of
                    intention to negotiate a trade agreement with Peru on Monday, December
                        29.<anchor n="76" xml:id="d448-f1"/></p>
                <p>For list of products to accompany public notice on which this country will
                    consider granting concessions to Peru, refer to instruction no. 446, of June 6,
                        1941.<anchor n="77" xml:id="d448-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d448-f1" n="76" xml:id="d448-f1-content">
                <p>The public notice was issued on December 29; see Department of State <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, January 3, 1942, p. 22.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d448-f2" n="77" xml:id="d448-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
